@page "/about-anvil"

<PageTitle>What is Anvil? | Anvil Store</PageTitle>
<section class="page-hero section-wrap about-hero">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A better starting point</p>
        <h1>Build the web<br /><em>with Anvil.</em></h1>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-copy">Anvil is a modern .NET application framework for building fast, maintainable server-rendered web applications with Razor, C#, and the tools you already know.</p>
</section>
<section class="section-wrap about-grid">
    <article class="about-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">In plain English</p>
        <h2>Everything you need to ship a real application.</h2>
        <p>Anvil gives your application a clear foundation instead of asking you to assemble every piece yourself. It brings together web UI, identity, persistence, background work, caching, observability, and more in a cohesive .NET stack.</p>
        <p>You keep the advantages of server-rendered HTML and C# while getting the structure needed for production software. There is no opaque platform to work around: your application remains yours, and its source stays close to the work you are doing.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://rudistorm.github.io/Anvil/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the Anvil documentation <span>↗</span></a>
    </article>
    <aside class="about-aside">
        <div class="about-point"><span>01</span><div><h3>Server-rendered by design</h3><p>Deliver useful HTML quickly and enhance the experience where it makes sense.</p></div></div>
        <div class="about-point"><span>02</span><div><h3>Built on .NET</h3><p>Use C#, Razor, ASP.NET Core, and the broader .NET ecosystem without leaving your application.</p></div></div>
        <div class="about-point"><span>03</span><div><h3>Made to be extended</h3><p>Start with a strong application shape, then change the code to fit your product.</p></div></div>
    </aside>
</section>
<section class="section-wrap about-store-callout">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this store exists</p>
        <h2>Start with working pieces, not an empty folder.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
        <p>These templates and providers are editable Anvil building blocks. Browse the source, learn from the implementation, and make it your own.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/templates">Explore the store <span>→</span></a>
    </div>
</section>
